Patches
- Review OpenBSD patches, especially %gs stubs and thread signals.
- Explore LEA + short %gs instruction patching for mimalloc/bun performance.

Features to investigate
- Executable path discovery (getexecpath): tools/tools.h, loader/main.c,
  server/unicode.c.
- Thread CPU times (get_thread_times): dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c.
- CPU performance and power information: SystemProcessorPerformanceInformation,
  IdleTime, HW_CPUSPEED and /dev/apm in dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c.
- Process information: review libprocstat-based code and OpenBSD KERN_PROC
  equivalents in dlls/ntdll/process.c and server/process.c.
- FAT filesystem handling (msdos/msdosfs): dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c.
- Removable device detection (is_device_removable): server/fd.c.
- Serial port discovery (/dev/cua* and /dev/cuau*): dlls/mountmgr.sys/unixlib.c.
- Native sndio audio backend.

Testing & fixes
- Broaden testing beyond games.
- Investigate tests failures and hangs.
- Fix signal handler reentrancy issues.

Packaging and maintenance
- Move Gecko/Mono to SUPDISTFILES; preserve test fetching and checksums.
  Or reconsider keeping tests.
- Use an LLVM headers package instead of the full source archive.
- Continue co-maintenance with Andrii Yukhymchak (NethIafin).
